OL,3,GNEWSARare Anglo-Saxon coin unearthed in
OL,4,AShetland
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe northernmost Anglo-Saxon coin found
OL,7,Fin the UK has been discovered in
OL,8,FShetland, say archaeologists.
OL,10,FA group of archaeologists and
OL,11,Fdetectorists uncovered the crux penny -
OL,12,Fwhich dates from the late 10th Century
OL,13,F- in Nesting, part of the east Shetland
OL,14,FMainland.
OL,16,FThe find suggests possible trading
OL,17,Froutes between Viking-controlled
OL,18,FShetland with Anglo-Saxons in England,
OL,19,For that it could be treasure from a
OL,20,FNorse raid.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
